Upstream-Name: Home Assistant (a client app for CyberdeckZero Launcher)
Upstream-Contact: OSRdesign <https://github.com/OSRdesign/cyberdeck-zero-apps>
Source: https://github.com/OSRdesign/cyberdeck-zero-apps/tree/main/apps/home-assistant
Comment: A client of a Home Assistant server on the local network, over Home
 Assistant's WebSocket and authentication APIs. It is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by the Home Assistant project; "Home Assistant" names the server it talks
 to. The icon is the app's own (a house with a signal), not a mark of that project.
 .
 The binary contains the LVGL based cp0_lvgl runtime of the CyberdeckZero Launcher
 (derived from the MIT-licensed launcher of M5Stack Technology CO LTD) and LVGL,
 and the QR Code generator library by Project Nayuki (C++ version 1.8.0, unchanged),
 all under the MIT licence, listed below.
 .
 libcurl is not shipped: the app opens the system's libcurl.so.4 (Debian package
 libcurl4t64, the curl licence, https://curl.se/docs/copyright.html) at run time.

